{title: 448 - O, When Shall I See Jesus}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Early Advent}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Em]O when shall I see Jesus, and reign with Him above,
[D]And shall hear the [C]trumpet [Em]sound in that [Am]morning?
[Em]And from [Bm]that [Em]flowing fountain drink everlasting [D/A]love!
[G]And shall hear the [Am]trumpet sound in [Em]that morning?

Refrain:
[Em]O, shout, [D/F#]glory! [G]For [D]I shall [G]mount above [C]the [Em]skies,
[D]When I hear [G/D]the trumpet sound [Am]in that [Em]morning.

Verse 2:
[Em]Gird on the gospel armor of faith and hope and love,
[D]And you'll hear the [C]trumpet [Em]sound in that [Am]morning.
[Em]And when [Bm]the [Em]combat's ended He'll carry [D]you above,
[G]And you'll hear the [Am]trumpet sound in [Em]that morning.

Verse 3:
[Em]Our ears shall hear with transport the host of heaven sing,
[D]And shall hear the [C]trumpet [Em]sound in that [Am]morning.
[Em]Our tongues shall chant the glories of [D]our immortal King.
[G]And shall hear the [Am]trumpet sound in [Em]that morning,
